# Material 3 Migration Scratchpad

## 🎯 Objective
Migrate the EventWish app from Material Components (Material 2) to Material 3 to leverage dynamic color theming, improved components, and better accessibility features.

## 🧩 Related Files
- app/build.gradle (update dependencies)
- app/src/main/res/values/themes.xml (update theme parent and attributes)
- app/src/main/res/values-night/themes.xml (create for dark theme support)
- app/src/main/res/values/colors.xml (update color system)
- app/src/main/res/values/styles.xml (update component styles)
- app/src/main/java/com/ds/eventwish/EventWishApplication.java (for applying dynamic colors)
- app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml (update application theme)
- Various layout XML files (update component references and attributes)

## ✅ Checklist
- [x] Update Material library dependency to latest version (already using 1.11.0)
- [x] Create a Material 3 theme extending Theme.Material3.DayNight
- [x] Create a night theme version for dark mode support
- [x] Update color system to use Material 3 color tokens
- [x] Update component styles to use Material 3 components
- [x] Add dynamic color support (optional, for Android 12+)
- [x] Fix critical theme issue in AndroidManifest.xml
- [ ] Test on different Android versions
- [ ] Test in both light and dark modes
- [ ] Verify accessibility compliance

## 🧠 Context
The app currently uses Material Components (Material 2) with a custom theme extending Theme.MaterialComponents.Light.NoActionBar. The app has extensive styling with custom colors, text appearances, and component styles. The migration to Material 3 will require updating these styles to match the Material 3 design system.

Material 3 introduces several changes:
1. New color system with dynamic color support
2. Updated component designs and behaviors
3. Better accessibility features
4. Improved dark theme support

## 📊 Implementation Progress

